00:38:43.980 --> 00:38:46.560
Because the guy I liked was really into watching
因为我喜欢的那个家伙非常喜欢看

981
00:38:47.080 --> 00:38:52.040
Bassmasters, watching people fish and talk about the hooks they used and the lures and the whatnot.
《巨鲈大师》，看人们钓鱼，谈论他们用的鱼钩、假饵之类的东西。

982
00:38:53.360 --> 00:38:54.740
These are the things you do.
这就是你会做的事。

983
00:38:54.920 --> 00:38:55.260
Yeah.
对。

984
00:38:55.340 --> 00:38:56.200
When you have a crush.
当你暗恋某人的时候。

985
00:38:56.440 --> 00:38:56.620
Yeah.
对。

986
00:38:56.820 --> 00:39:00.300
When all of a sudden, this guy is like, I think on Sunday, I'm going to watch Bassmasters.
当这家伙突然说，我想周日我要看《巨鲈大师》。

987
00:39:00.400 --> 00:39:01.460
I'm like, oh, yeah, it's so great.
我就说，哦，对啊，太棒了。

988
00:39:01.660 --> 00:39:03.560
That guy, the host, he's hilarious.
那家伙，那个主持人，太逗了。

989
00:39:03.940 --> 00:39:05.520
And then you're like, who is the host?
然后你在想，谁是主持人？

990
00:39:05.780 --> 00:39:07.680
There is no host of Bassmasters.
《巨鲈大师》根本没有主持人。

991
00:39:07.740 --> 00:39:08.940
What is Bassmasters?
什么是《巨鲈大师》？

992
00:39:09.840 --> 00:39:12.780
And you couldn't Google back then because it was just invented.
而且那时候你没法用谷歌搜索，因为刚发明没多久。

993
00:39:12.960 --> 00:39:13.460
I know.
我知道。

994
00:39:13.860 --> 00:39:14.200
Yeah.
对。

995
00:39:14.280 --> 00:39:15.560
It wasn't invented yet.
还没发明出来呢。

996
00:39:15.780 --> 00:39:16.720
There was no internet.
当时还没有互联网。

997
00:39:17.160 --> 00:39:18.700
I will never let that one go.
我永远不会放过这个梗。

998
00:39:18.820 --> 00:39:19.080
I know.
我知道。

999
00:39:19.180 --> 00:39:19.680
It's too fun.
太好玩了。

1000
00:39:19.680 --> 00:39:20.000
Clearly.
显然。

1001
00:39:20.180 --> 00:39:20.680
It's too fun.
太有意思了。

1002
00:39:20.680 --> 00:39:22.240
It's one of my favorite bits now.
这现在成了我最喜欢的桥段之一。

1003
00:39:24.040 --> 00:39:29.700
While Michael is still sitting in the chair upstairs, trying to get people to sit on his lap,
当迈克尔还坐在楼上的椅子上，试图让人坐在他腿上时，

1004
00:39:29.840 --> 00:39:36.360
he is now like wrestling Ryan onto his lap while saying, I need this, I need this.
他现在就像是把瑞安摔到自己腿上，还一边说，我需要这个，我需要这个。

1005
00:39:36.360 --> 00:39:41.780
Claire and Mindy also talked in the commentary that when Jim steps in and is like, hey,
克莱尔和敏迪在随笔解说里也聊到，当吉姆介入并说，嘿，

1006
00:39:42.800 --> 00:39:47.620
you know, Michael, you can't, you know, you can't grab someone in the office and say,
你知道的，迈克尔，你不能，你知道，你不能在办公室里抓住某个人然后说，

1007
00:39:47.800 --> 00:39:48.540
I need this.
我需要这个。

1008
00:39:48.540 --> 00:39:50.420
While forcing them onto your lap.
同时把他们强行按在你的腿上。

1009
00:39:50.680 --> 00:39:52.320
It makes me laugh out loud every time.
每次都让我哈哈大笑。

1010
00:39:52.520 --> 00:39:53.640
John's delivery is so good.
约翰的演绎太棒了。

1011
00:39:53.920 --> 00:39:57.140
They shared on the commentary that he kept laughing in so many takes.
他们在解说里分享说，他在很多镜头里都忍不住笑场。

1012
00:39:57.600 --> 00:39:58.420
That's the thing.
就是这样。

1013
00:39:58.560 --> 00:40:03.120
Like when you know something is funny, even though you have to deliver it, it like, it tickles
就像当你明知某件事很好笑时，尽管你必须把它演出来，它还是会，它会让

1014
00:40:03.120 --> 00:40:04.240
you while you're doing it.
你在演的时候觉得很好玩。

1015
00:40:04.420 --> 00:40:04.660
Yes.
是的。

1016
00:40:05.700 --> 00:40:11.700
This scene is going to end with Michael putting his Santa hat into the punch bowl and storming
这个场景将以迈克尔把他的圣诞老人帽子放进潘趣酒碗里然后气冲冲地

1017
00:40:11.700 --> 00:40:12.080
out.
离开而告终。

1018
00:40:12.220 --> 00:40:12.800
So rude.
太粗鲁了。

1019
00:40:13.180 --> 00:40:16.020
Mindy talked about something in the commentary I thought was really interesting.
敏迪在解说里聊到了一件事，我觉得非常有意思。

1020
00:40:16.280 --> 00:40:20.880
She said at eight minutes, 39 seconds, when Michael makes his big announcement that he wants
她说在八分三十九秒时，当迈克尔发布他的重大声明，说他希望

1021
00:40:20.880 --> 00:40:22.860
a vote on who is the true Santa.
就谁才是真正的圣诞老人进行投票时。

1022
00:40:23.640 --> 00:40:28.880
Mindy said, and I'm quoting her, one of the great legacies of the show is the announcements
敏迪说，我引用她的话，这部剧最伟大的遗产之一就是迈克尔办公室

1023
00:40:28.880 --> 00:40:30.580
outside of Michael's office.
外面的那些重大声明。

1024
00:40:30.880 --> 00:40:34.740
She goes on to say, I used to call it Act Break Alley.
她接着说，我以前把它叫做幕间休息巷。

1025
00:40:35.020 --> 00:40:39.300
The writers would have Michael come out of his office, make an announcement, and that
编剧们会让迈克尔从办公室出来，发表一个声明，而这

1026
00:40:39.300 --> 00:40:40.720
would often lead to the Act Break.
通常会引出幕间休息。

1027
00:40:41.180 --> 00:40:42.960
And that's exactly what happens here.
这里发生的正是如此。

1028
00:40:43.080 --> 00:40:43.560
It's true.
确实如此。

1029
00:40:43.960 --> 00:40:46.620
So you got a little Act Break Alley there.
所以你们在那里有了一条小小的幕间休息巷。

1030
00:40:47.860 --> 00:40:52.280
Dwight is convinced that his secret Santa is sending him pieces of a gun.
德怀特确信他的秘密圣诞老人送给他的是一把枪的零件。

1031
00:40:52.700 --> 00:40:55.160
But this last piece doesn't make any sense.
但最后这个零件根本说不通。

1032
00:40:55.460 --> 00:40:56.860
Why did they send him a dial?
为什么他们要送他一个表盘？

1033
00:40:57.040 --> 00:40:58.260
They should have sent him a trigger.
他们应该送他一个扳机才对。

1034
00:40:59.000 --> 00:41:01.740
And Meredith and Phyllis are like, why do you think it's a gun?
而梅雷迪思和菲利斯则觉得，你为什么会觉得这是枪？

1035
00:41:02.420 --> 00:41:07.540
And then Stanley has a great line where he says, unless the missing piece is a gun,
然后斯坦利有一句绝妙的台词，他说，除非缺少的那个零件是一把枪，

1036
00:41:07.740 --> 00:41:08.920
you don't have a gun.
否则你根本没有枪。

1037
00:41:09.960 --> 00:41:11.980
I don't know why that tickles me so much.
我不知道为什么这让我觉得这么好笑。

1038
00:41:12.360 --> 00:41:13.700
His delivery was so good.
他的演绎太棒了。

1039
00:41:14.220 --> 00:41:16.500
We got a fan question from Beth G.
我们收到了来自华盛顿州奥林匹亚的

1040
00:41:16.700 --> 00:41:17.740
in Olympia, Washington.
贝丝·G的粉丝提问。

1041
00:41:18.100 --> 00:41:24.980
Who came up with the list of Dwight's speculations on what his Christmas present might be as he
是谁想出了德怀特关于他的圣诞礼物可能是什么的种种猜测清单，就在他

1042
00:41:24.980 --> 00:41:25.640
builds it?
组装的时候？

1043
00:41:25.800 --> 00:41:28.420
You know, he has that piece of paper with the liSt.
你知道的，他手里拿着那张写着清单的纸。

1044
00:41:28.420 --> 00:41:32.020
And Beth said, I never noticed that Speculum was on the liSt.
贝丝说，我以前从没注意到清单上居然有“窥阴器”。

1045
00:41:32.180 --> 00:41:36.240
But during a recent rewatch, I noticed and almost died laughing.
但在最近的一次重温中，我注意到了，差点笑死。

1046
00:41:36.680 --> 00:41:40.880
So I found a list of all the things that Dwight thinks.
所以我找到了德怀特想到的所有东西的清单。

1047
00:41:41.040 --> 00:41:42.540
This is what's on his piece of paper.
这就是他那张纸上写的内容。

1048
00:41:43.020 --> 00:41:45.640
In answer to your question, Beth, this would be the writers.
回答你的问题，贝丝，这应该是编剧们想的。

1049
00:41:45.940 --> 00:41:47.460
The writers would have come up with this liSt.
这肯定是编剧们想出来的清单。

1050
00:41:47.460 --> 00:41:51.920
Phil Shea would have gone to the writers and said, what do you want me to write on this piece
菲尔·希伊当时肯定会去找编剧们说，你们想让我在这张纸上写什么

1051
00:41:51.920 --> 00:41:52.980
of paper for Dwight?
给德怀特准备的纸张？

1052
00:41:53.120 --> 00:41:53.300
Right.
没错。

1053
00:41:53.520 --> 00:41:57.640
And he would have had to write this list over and over and over and over again on various
而且他不得不把这个单子在一张又一张、各种各样的

1054
00:41:57.640 --> 00:42:01.580
pads of paper because every take, Rain was going to scratch one out.
便签纸上写了一遍、一遍、又一遍、又一遍，因为每一个镜头雷恩都要划掉一个。

1055
00:42:01.780 --> 00:42:05.260
So here was the list of things that Dwight thought this might be.
所以这就是德怀特认为这可能是的东西的单子。

1056
00:42:05.260 --> 00:42:16.060
An aardvark trap, beaver trap, gun, chipmunk trap, possum trap, skunk trap, lobster trap, man trap,
土豚陷阱、海狸陷阱、枪、花栗鼠陷阱、负鼠陷阱、臭鼬陷阱、龙虾陷阱、捕人器、

1057
00:42:16.760 --> 00:42:19.960
lathe, abdominizer, speculum.
车床、腹肌锻炼器、窥阴器。

1058
00:42:20.880 --> 00:42:25.640
He was mostly convinced it was some sort of trap, an animal trap.
他基本上确信这是某种陷阱，一种动物陷阱。

1059
00:42:27.660 --> 00:42:31.480
Santa Phyllis is now going to do the tree lighting reveal.
圣诞老人菲利丝现在要开始点亮圣诞树了。

1060
00:42:31.660 --> 00:42:33.820
And it's so festive and cheery.
而且这太喜庆、太欢乐了。

1061
00:42:33.820 --> 00:42:35.200
I love Phyllis in this scene.
我好喜欢这场戏里的菲利丝。

1062
00:42:35.320 --> 00:42:35.820
I know.
我知道。

1063
00:42:35.980 --> 00:42:37.120
I absolutely love it.
我真的超级喜欢。

1064
00:42:37.340 --> 00:42:39.660
Michael is starting to get real sour.
迈克尔开始变得很不爽了。

1065
00:42:40.180 --> 00:42:40.900
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

1066
00:42:41.340 --> 00:42:47.680
So he has this talking head where he says, I don't need a lot for Christmas, like diamonds
所以他有一段独白说，我圣诞节不需要太多东西，比如钻石

1067
00:42:47.680 --> 00:42:49.760
or brooch, pendants.
或胸针、吊坠。

1068
00:42:50.500 --> 00:42:52.220
He just wants to be Santa.
他只想当圣诞老人。

1069
00:42:52.580 --> 00:42:58.160
And this whole time, he is, like, reversing his Santa costume.
而在这个过程中，他一直在把他的圣诞老人服装反过来穿。

1070
00:42:58.460 --> 00:43:03.440
Taking this decorative Christmas robe off his credenza, making it into a belt.
把写字台上的装饰性圣诞长袍脱下来，把它做成腰带。

1071
00:43:03.620 --> 00:43:06.620
I want to give a shout out to Steve's skills right here.
我在这里要为史蒂夫的演技点个赞。

1072
00:43:06.740 --> 00:43:08.300
I put it in my document.
我把它记在我的文档里了。

1073
00:43:08.300 --> 00:43:11.880
I need everyone to appreciate how hard this is to do.
我需要所有人都体会到这有多难做到。

1074
00:43:12.020 --> 00:43:13.260
Yes, I wrote it, too.
对，我也写下来了。

1075
00:43:13.380 --> 00:43:15.060
I put two little stars by it.
我在旁边画了两个小星星。

1076
00:43:15.140 --> 00:43:17.280
I said, go to nine minutes, 52 seconds.
我说，到九分五十二秒那里。

1077
00:43:17.580 --> 00:43:19.700
Michael goes from Santa to Jesus.
迈克尔从圣诞老人变成了耶稣。

1078
00:43:19.960 --> 00:43:25.920
And Steve had to do all the dialogue, change his outfit, put the belts on in one shot.
而且史蒂夫必须在同一个镜头里完成所有的对话、换衣服、系腰带。

1079
00:43:26.060 --> 00:43:27.160
There are no cutaways.
中间没有任何剪辑切换。

1080
00:43:27.840 --> 00:43:29.280
This is truly amazing.
这真的很惊人。

1081
00:43:29.500 --> 00:43:35.640
I cannot express to you how hard it is to do even ordinary business while you're acting.
我无法向你们表达，在演戏的同时还要做普通的日常杂务有多难。

1082
00:43:35.640 --> 00:43:44.560
How many times would I have to do a scene where I'm supposed to walk in with a bag of groceries, set it down, and take some items out of the bag?
我有多少次要拍一场戏，要求我提着一袋杂货走进来，把它放下，再从袋子里拿几样东西出来？

1083
00:43:45.020 --> 00:43:47.700
Suddenly, I am incapable of doing that action.
突然之间，我就不会做这个动作了。

1084
00:43:47.700 --> 00:43:53.040
I multitask in my kitchen constantly, and I'm always thinking about it, too.
我在厨房里经常一心多用，而且我干活的时候也总是在想这个。

1085
00:43:53.220 --> 00:43:59.120
Like, as I'm, like, shutting the fridge with my foot while scrambling an egg and drinking coffee and, like,
比如，当我就像是用脚关上冰箱门，同时炒着鸡蛋、喝着咖啡，还,

1086
00:43:59.640 --> 00:44:07.620
organizing some homework papers in the morning and holding a conversation, I think to myself, if this was written out for me, I could never do it.
在早晨整理一些作业文件并维持对话时，我心里想，如果这段戏是专门写给我的，我绝对演不出来。

1087
00:44:07.720 --> 00:44:08.640
I don't know what it is.
我不知道这是怎么回事。

1088
00:44:08.640 --> 00:44:11.760
It's so hard just to memorize your lines and say them truthfully.
光是记住台词并真诚地把它们说出来就已经太难了。

1089
00:44:12.500 --> 00:44:16.060
This amount of business is—people should study it.
这种杂务的量——人们真该好好研究一下。

1090
00:44:16.140 --> 00:44:17.040
He does such a good job.
他做得太棒了。

1091
00:44:17.380 --> 00:44:18.860
And with comic timing!
而且还有喜剧节奏！

1092
00:44:18.860 --> 00:44:19.600
I know.
我知道。

1093
00:44:19.720 --> 00:44:29.360
I always think of this when I would watch shows like ER or Grey's Anatomy, when they have the gurney flying through the hallway, and they're yelling out all of this medical jargon,
我每次看《急诊室的故事》或《实习医生格蕾》这样的剧时都会想到这一点，当急救推车在走廊里飞奔，他们在大喊大叫各种医学术语时，

1094
00:44:29.560 --> 00:44:33.180
like, stick me this gossip, blah, blah, blah, and they're, like, having to do all this action.
比如，给我这个纱布，巴拉巴拉巴拉，然后他们还得做所有这些动作。

1095
00:44:33.360 --> 00:44:38.400
I'm, like, well, that'll be a job I never have because that's a lot of talking and moving at the same time.
我想，好吧，那我永远也干不了这工作，因为这又得说话又得同时移动，实在太难了。

1096
00:44:38.840 --> 00:44:39.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1097
00:44:39.420 --> 00:44:40.500
I won't be able to do it.
我可做不到。

1098
00:44:40.660 --> 00:44:42.700
Lots of business is hard to do.
各种繁杂的动作很难处理。

1099
00:44:42.840 --> 00:44:43.380
Lots of business.
太多的杂务了。

1100
00:44:43.460 --> 00:44:45.500
Because then also you have to, like, match it.
因为接着你还得把动作连贯起来。

1101
00:44:45.640 --> 00:44:46.660
Yeah, every time.
对，每次都这样。

1102
00:44:48.860 --> 00:44:50.240
We were both very impressed.
我们俩都印象深刻。

1103
00:44:50.460 --> 00:44:51.180
We were.
确实如此。

1104
00:44:51.320 --> 00:44:55.880
We were also cast on the perfect show because we often didn't have to do a lot of business.
而且我们被分配到了一个完美的节目，因为我们经常不用演太多剧情。

1105
00:44:56.120 --> 00:44:57.020
We were just at our desk.
我们只需坐在办公桌前就行。

1106
00:44:57.360 --> 00:44:57.580
True.
没错。

1107
00:44:58.380 --> 00:45:00.320
Michael returns to the bullpen now.
迈克尔现在回到了大办公区。

1108
00:45:00.900 --> 00:45:02.320
He's Jesus ChriSt.
他简直就是救世主。

1109
00:45:02.720 --> 00:45:03.840
Angela applauds.
安吉拉鼓掌。

1110
00:45:04.080 --> 00:45:05.500
She's the only one applauding.
她是唯一一个鼓掌的人。

1111
00:45:05.720 --> 00:45:07.880
I mean, finally, as far as she's concerned.
我的意思是，对她而言，这简直千呼万唤始出来。

1112
00:45:08.000 --> 00:45:08.220
Right.
对。

1113
00:45:08.400 --> 00:45:10.640
Finally, we have a real Christmas party.
终于，我们有了一个真正的圣诞派对。

1114
00:45:10.880 --> 00:45:14.120
I went to the script to see if me applauding was written in the script.
我特意去查了剧本，看我鼓掌是不是剧本里写好的。

1115
00:45:14.220 --> 00:45:14.780
It was.
确实是。

1116
00:45:15.020 --> 00:45:17.100
It says, Angela claps.
上面写着，安吉拉鼓掌。

1117
00:45:17.100 --> 00:45:19.100
Well, lady, I think we should take a break.
好了，女士们，我觉得我们该休息一下了。

1118
00:45:19.220 --> 00:45:26.580
But before we do, I just want to quickly bring up this moment in the break room where Andy has asked Phyllis, please do not tell Aaron I am her secret Santa.
但在我们休息之前，我只想迅速提一下休息室里的这个时刻：安迪要求菲利斯千万别告诉安伦他是她的秘密圣诞老人。

1119
00:45:26.900 --> 00:45:28.660
And she says, okay, I won't.
然后她说，好的，我不会说。

1120
00:45:28.860 --> 00:45:30.060
I'll say it's Michael.
我会说是迈克尔。

1121
00:45:30.360 --> 00:45:31.440
Andy's like, great.
安迪一副太好了的表情。

1122
00:45:31.700 --> 00:45:31.960
Whatever.
无所谓。

1123
00:45:32.260 --> 00:45:34.200
Phyllis can throw Michael under the bus.
菲利斯可以把迈克尔当替罪羊卖了。

1124
00:45:34.620 --> 00:45:35.960
She's like, I'm going for it.
她一副豁出去了的样子。

1125
00:45:36.020 --> 00:45:37.340
Well, listen, he deserves it.
听着，他活该。

1126
00:45:37.360 --> 00:45:37.820
I know.
我知道。

1127
00:45:37.820 --> 00:45:38.620
I know.
我知道。

1128
00:45:38.620 --> 00:45:40.560
All right.
行吧。

1129
00:45:40.720 --> 00:45:42.580
We'll take a break and be right back.
我们休息一下，马上回来。

1130
00:45:52.560 --> 00:45:54.320
Aaron are singing some Christmas carols.
安伦正在唱几首圣诞颂歌。

1131
00:45:54.780 --> 00:45:58.380
I want you guys to know there was a whole lot more singing that got cut out.
我想让你们知道，其实还有一大堆歌唱片段被剪掉了。

1132
00:45:58.560 --> 00:45:58.780
Really?
真的吗？

1133
00:45:59.000 --> 00:45:59.300
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1134
00:45:59.700 --> 00:46:04.500
And while they're singing, Pam is going to ask Oscar if he's talked to Matt.
就在他们唱歌的时候，帕姆要问奥斯卡有没有跟马特聊过。

1135
00:46:04.900 --> 00:46:12.960
And then she is going into full matchmaker mode and she is just going to talk up Oscar's pate.
然后她就进入了全方位的红娘模式，开始极力夸奖奥斯卡的秃顶。

1136
00:46:12.960 --> 00:46:15.200
How many times do I say pate?
我说了多少次秃顶？

1137
00:46:15.640 --> 00:46:17.060
You're so awkward.
你太尴尬了。

1138
00:46:17.280 --> 00:46:18.500
It's so cringy.
简直社死。

1139
00:46:19.060 --> 00:46:22.000
Pam is just so delighted to be a matchmaker.
帕姆对于当红娘感到非常高兴。

1140
00:46:22.260 --> 00:46:22.580
I know.
我知道。

1141
00:46:22.660 --> 00:46:23.920
It was really fun to play.
演起来真的很有趣。

1142
00:46:24.140 --> 00:46:27.880
We had a fan question from Robbie V in South Korea.
我们收到了来自韩国的罗比·V的粉丝提问。

1143
00:46:28.200 --> 00:46:30.500
Who played Matt from The Warehouse?
仓库里的马特是谁演的？

1144
00:46:30.760 --> 00:46:33.920
Guys, Matt was played by Sam Daly.
各位，马特由山姆·戴利饰演。

1145
00:46:34.380 --> 00:46:40.720
In addition to The Office, Sam has appeared on such shows as The Magicians, NCIS, Heart of Dixie,
除了《办公室》，山姆还出演过《魔法师》、《海军罪案调查处》、《南国医恋》等剧集，

1146
00:46:40.720 --> 00:46:45.460
and in recurring roles on Madam Secretary and The Undercovers,
并在《国务卿女士》和《卧底情侣》中担任常驻角色，

1147
00:46:45.480 --> 00:46:48.020
and most recently on Bull.
最近还出演了《庭审专家》。

1148
00:46:48.480 --> 00:46:51.680
He is also the son of actor Tim Daly.
他也是演员蒂姆·戴利的儿子。

1149
00:46:51.900 --> 00:46:52.800
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

1150
00:46:52.800 --> 00:46:57.140
I was so excited when he was on set because I loved Wings.
他到片场时我超级兴奋，因为我特别喜欢《展翅高飞》。

1151
00:46:57.320 --> 00:46:58.100
Loved Wings.
我超喜欢《 Wings 》。

1152
00:46:58.320 --> 00:46:59.640
I watched every episode.
我每集都看。

1153
00:46:59.740 --> 00:47:02.100
I even went to a taping, you guys.
我甚至还去看过现场录制呢，你们大家。

1154
00:47:02.240 --> 00:47:02.660
You did?
真的吗？

1155
00:47:02.860 --> 00:47:03.160
Yes.
对。

1156
00:47:03.260 --> 00:47:04.040
I came out to L.A.
我来过洛杉矶

1157
00:47:04.100 --> 00:47:05.980
to visit like years before I lived here.
就在我搬来这里的好几年前，来这儿参观。

1158
00:47:06.160 --> 00:47:08.580
And I went to a taping of Wings.
然后我去看了《 Wings 》的现场录制。

1159
00:47:08.740 --> 00:47:10.120
I did that same thing, too.
我也做过同样的事。

1160
00:47:10.120 --> 00:47:10.880
I came out.
我来过。

1161
00:47:11.060 --> 00:47:15.800
It was like a special workshop for people who were interested in the biz.
那就像是一个专门为对这行感兴趣的人办的特别工作坊。

1162
00:47:16.040 --> 00:47:21.600
It was through UCLA, I think, because we stayed on the campus, and they took us all around.
好像是通过加州大学洛杉矶分校办的，因为我们住在校园里，他们带我们到处参观。

1163
00:47:21.920 --> 00:47:25.500
And one of the things we got to do was go to a live television taping.
我们能做的事情之一就是去观看电视节目的现场录制。

1164
00:47:25.600 --> 00:47:26.820
I was fascinated.
我当时迷得不行。

1165
00:47:27.140 --> 00:47:28.200
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

1166
00:47:28.340 --> 00:47:29.680
I was coming out to visit.
我是来这里探亲访友的。

1167
00:47:29.820 --> 00:47:35.160
My friend's brother was going to college here, and we came and visited him, and he took us to a live taping.
我朋友的兄弟当时在这儿上大学，我们来探望他，他带我们去看了现场录制。

1168
00:47:35.780 --> 00:47:44.300
Crystal Bernard, during an act break, you know, because it was like a four-camera show where you're in an audience, and they would have, like, breaks.
克里斯蒂尔·伯纳德在幕间休息的时候，你知道的，因为那是那种有观众的四机位情景喜剧，他们会有那种休息时间。

1169
00:47:44.300 --> 00:47:49.040
She came up with her guitar and sang a whole song, and she was such a good singer.
她拿着吉他走过来，唱了一整首歌，她歌唱得真好听。

1170
00:47:49.380 --> 00:47:50.460
That is so sweet.
那太甜了。

1171
00:47:50.560 --> 00:47:51.800
You know, that's a nice caSt.
你知道的，那是个很好的演员阵容。

1172
00:47:52.260 --> 00:47:52.540
Yeah.
对啊。

1173
00:47:53.040 --> 00:48:00.600
When I did my taping of that 70s show, the entire cast, after the show was over, went out to the audience and signed autographs.
当我录制《That 70s Show》时，整个剧组在节目结束后，走到观众席去签名了。

1174
00:48:00.700 --> 00:48:03.820
And, I mean, this was, like, year, like, six or something.
我的意思是，那大约是第六季左右吧。

1175
00:48:04.280 --> 00:48:05.460
I was so impressed.
我印象极其深刻。

1176
00:48:05.460 --> 00:48:09.140
Well, we were very excited to have Sam on set.
总之，山姆来到片场让我们非常兴奋。

1177
00:48:09.340 --> 00:48:09.960
We were.
确实如此。

1178
00:48:10.240 --> 00:48:14.280
Sam did an interview with BleepMag.com.
山姆接受了 BleepMag.com 的采访。

1179
00:48:14.380 --> 00:48:16.260
Angela, thank you for forwarding me this.
安吉拉，谢谢你转发给我这个。

1180
00:48:16.440 --> 00:48:22.100
They asked him if he gets recognized for being Matt on our show.
他们问他是否因为在我们剧里扮演马特而被认出来。

1181
00:48:22.100 --> 00:48:23.980
And he said, yes.
他说，是的。

1182
00:48:24.460 --> 00:48:30.000
Nine times out of ten, if he gets recognized, it's for having been on The Office.
十有八九，如果他被认出来，都是因为曾参演过《办公室》。

1183
00:48:30.660 --> 00:48:36.980
He also said, quote, it was the first show I'd seen every episode of when I went to work on it.
他还说，原话是：这是我参演之前就看过每一集的第一个节目。

1184
00:48:37.180 --> 00:48:40.720
I knew where to go in The Office and who sat where and everything.
我知道在《办公室》里该去哪，谁坐在哪，以及所有的事情。

1185
00:48:41.000 --> 00:48:42.940
It was such an incredible experience.
那真是一次不可思议的经历。

1186
00:48:43.480 --> 00:48:48.160
It was supposed to be a tiny role, but it turned into a recurring guest spot for a few episodes.
本来应该是个很小的角色，但后来变成了一个客串好几集的常驻角色。

1187
00:48:48.500 --> 00:48:53.320
I'll never take that for granted, and being around all those other actors was a blessing.
我永远不会把这视为理所当然，能和所有这些其他演员在一起是一种福气。

1188
00:48:53.740 --> 00:48:55.300
Sam, you were a blessing.
山姆，你才是我们的福气。

1189
00:48:55.540 --> 00:48:56.800
You were so delightful.
你太讨人喜欢了。

1190
00:48:57.140 --> 00:48:59.400
And he is going to be in two more episodes.
而且他还将在另外两集中出现。

1191
00:48:59.400 --> 00:49:01.060
We just really liked him so much.
我们真的是太喜欢他了。

1192
00:49:01.420 --> 00:49:03.480
Well, Jen, I have two things to share about this scene.
好吧，詹，关于这个场景我有两件事要分享。

1193
00:49:03.740 --> 00:49:05.840
So we see Matt from the warehouse upstairs.
我们看到仓库的马特上楼了。

1194
00:49:06.180 --> 00:49:07.920
Did you notice the other warehouse workers?
你注意到其他的仓库工人了吗？

1195
00:49:08.180 --> 00:49:11.840
Yes, I noticed Madge and all the guys are at this party.
是的，我注意到麦奇和所有工人都来参加这个派对。

1196
00:49:12.500 --> 00:49:15.380
Well, there was a whole runner that was cut from the episode.
其实这集里删掉了一条完整的贯穿剧情。

1197
00:49:15.440 --> 00:49:21.320
It is in the extended producer's cut where Michael goes down to the warehouse and invites all of them up to the party.
在加长导演剪辑版里，迈克尔去了仓库，邀请他们所有人都上来参加派对。

1198
00:49:22.220 --> 00:49:23.660
It does not go over well.
结果很不顺利。

1199
00:49:24.060 --> 00:49:24.300
Why?
为什么？

1200
00:49:24.900 --> 00:49:28.380
Jim is annoyed because he did not plan to feed that many people.
吉姆很不爽，因为他根本没打算喂饱那么多人。

1201
00:49:28.700 --> 00:49:29.140
Oh.
哦。

1202
00:49:29.400 --> 00:49:32.940
I thought it was really cute because he was all of a sudden concerned about food.
我觉得这真的挺可爱的，因为他突然开始关心起吃的来了。

1203
00:49:33.160 --> 00:49:39.120
The rest of the office is grumpy because the warehouse workers start eating everything, kind of take over.
办公室的其他人都很不高兴，因为仓库员工开始吃掉所有东西，有点像占领了这里。

1204
00:49:39.660 --> 00:49:48.860
Angela has a talking head where she says she can hardly pretend to like the people in the actual office, let alone all the extra people now.
安吉拉有个单采镜头，说她对办公室里的这些人连装作喜欢都很难，更别说现在还有这么多额外的人了。

1205
00:49:48.860 --> 00:49:55.120
There is a scene in the conference room where we learn that Madge has a nickname, Garfield.
会议室里有一场戏，我们得知马奇有个外号叫加菲猫。

1206
00:49:55.540 --> 00:49:57.460
Oh, because she loves lasagna?
哦，是因为她喜欢千层面吗？

1207
00:49:57.680 --> 00:49:59.080
Because she loves lasagna.
因为她喜欢千层面。

1208
00:49:59.240 --> 00:50:01.520
And when she sees it, she has to eat it all.
而且当她看到它时，她必须把它全吃光。

1209
00:50:01.700 --> 00:50:10.640
This results in a scene where she eats the entire lasagna that Pam brought while the warehouse guys are chanting, Garfield, Garfield, Garfield.
这导致了一场戏：当仓库的伙计们在一边高喊“加菲猫，加菲猫，加菲猫”时，她把潘带来的整盘千层面都吃光了。

1210
00:50:11.540 --> 00:50:12.060
Amazing.
太绝了。

1211
00:50:12.060 --> 00:50:17.680
Yes, there were so many extra scenes of the warehouse people driving everyone in the bullpen crazy.
对，有好多仓库员工把开放式办公区所有人折腾疯了的加戏。

1212
00:50:18.180 --> 00:50:25.380
The second thing I want to share is on the commentary, Mindy and Ellie talked about how when they met Sam Daly, who played Matt,
我要分享的第二件事是，在评论音轨里，敏迪和艾莉谈到当她们遇到饰演马特的萨姆·戴利时，

1213
00:50:25.680 --> 00:50:30.600
they got so tickled because they thought Sam and Ellie looked a lot alike in real life.
她们觉得特别好笑，因为她们觉得萨姆和艾莉在现实生活中长得非常像。

1214
00:50:30.820 --> 00:50:32.440
Like they could be brother and sister?
就像他们可能是亲兄妹一样？

1215
00:50:32.440 --> 00:50:36.180
Yes, so I did a side-by-side and I want to show you.
对，所以我做了个对比照，想给你看看。

1216
00:50:36.900 --> 00:50:38.360
All right, Jenna, look at this.
好了，珍娜，看这个。

1217
00:50:38.500 --> 00:50:39.400
I'll put it in stories.
我会把它发到快拍里。

1218
00:50:39.700 --> 00:50:40.620
I see it.
我看到了。

1219
00:50:41.780 --> 00:50:43.120
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1220
00:50:44.520 --> 00:50:46.280
They definitely could be family.
他们绝对可以是一家子。

1221
00:50:46.560 --> 00:50:47.140
I know.
我懂。

1222
00:50:48.240 --> 00:50:52.740
So I guess this is something Ellie was tickled about, Ellie and Mindy, during the week of filming.
所以我想这是艾莉在拍摄那周觉得很好笑的一件事，艾莉和敏迪。

1223
00:50:54.320 --> 00:50:56.620
Michael is very cranky.
迈克尔非常暴躁。

1224
00:50:57.420 --> 00:51:08.720
He has, like, sat down kind of in the very middle of the party with a microphone, and he is narrating the gifts that are being handed out.
他，呃，坐在派对的正中央，拿着一个麦克风，在旁白解说正在分发的礼物。

1225
00:51:08.980 --> 00:51:11.200
Yeah, he's doing, like, snarky commentary.
对，他在做那种带讽刺意味的解说。

1226
00:51:11.600 --> 00:51:11.840
Yeah.
对。

1227
00:51:13.020 --> 00:51:15.940
Angela gets some fabric.
安吉拉收到了一些布料。

1228
00:51:15.960 --> 00:51:17.200
Some gray fabric.
一些灰色的布料。

1229
00:51:17.480 --> 00:51:18.780
She is so touched.
她好感动。

1230
00:51:18.920 --> 00:51:19.220
I know.
我知道。

1231
00:51:19.400 --> 00:51:21.020
This person really knew her well.
送礼这个人真的很了解她。

1232
00:51:21.600 --> 00:51:24.880
Michael says now she can make another dress that goes past her feet.
迈克尔说现在她可以再做一件拖地长裙了。

1233
00:51:26.620 --> 00:51:35.420
It is also during this snarky commentary that Michael reveals that Andy is Aaron's secret Santa.
也正是在这段刻薄的解说中，迈克尔透露安迪是艾伦的秘密圣诞老人。

1234
00:51:36.180 --> 00:51:36.820
Oof.
噢。

1235
00:51:37.400 --> 00:51:38.040
Oh, man.
天哪。

1236
00:51:38.620 --> 00:51:40.160
Aaron does not look happy.
艾伦看起来很不高兴。

1237
00:51:40.940 --> 00:51:46.700
Michael continues to spiral, so he calls David Wallace, and he has one of my favorite lines.
迈克尔继续情绪崩溃，于是他打电话给大卫·华莱士，并且他有一句我最喜欢的台词。

1238
00:51:46.880 --> 00:51:50.660
He says, a woman has you slurped his role as Santa.
他说，一个女人让你抢了她圣诞老人的角色。

1239
00:51:50.880 --> 00:51:51.240
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1240
00:51:51.680 --> 00:51:52.560
That's right.
没错。

1241
00:51:52.860 --> 00:51:55.240
He also says, guess who I'm dressed as?
他还说，猜猜我打扮成了谁？

1242
00:51:55.800 --> 00:52:01.860
And I love David Wallace's response because he says, either you tell me or I'm hanging up.
我特别喜欢大卫·华莱士的反应，因为他说，要么你告诉我，要么我就挂电话。

1243
00:52:02.100 --> 00:52:04.820
Like, I'm not guessing what you're dressed as.
就像，我才不猜你打扮成了谁。

1244
00:52:04.860 --> 00:52:05.180
I'm not doing this now.
我这会儿可不干这事。

1245
00:52:05.480 --> 00:52:10.600
Well, David said this is a really bad time and asked for Stephanie, his assistant, to step off.
嗯，大卫说现在真不是时候，并让他的助理斯蒂芬妮先出去。

1246
00:52:11.360 --> 00:52:11.660
Yes.
对。

1247
00:52:12.260 --> 00:52:15.500
And then Aaron also needs to get off the phone.
然后艾伦也需要挂电话。

1248
00:52:15.680 --> 00:52:17.540
Michael's like, have they always been here?
迈克尔一副“他们一直都在这儿吗”的样子。

1249
00:52:19.160 --> 00:52:26.060
David tells Michael that the company has a buyer, and he and Alan are out of work.
大卫告诉迈克尔公司有了收购方，他和艾伦失业了。

1250
00:52:26.180 --> 00:52:27.760
Like, just, you know what?
就像，干脆，你知道吗？

1251
00:52:28.200 --> 00:52:29.460
Everyone's going to be gone.
所有人都要走了。

1252
00:52:29.920 --> 00:52:30.340
Everyone.
所有人。

1253
00:52:31.140 --> 00:52:32.300
Michael hears that.
迈克尔听到了。

1254
00:52:33.140 --> 00:52:34.260
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1255
00:52:34.580 --> 00:52:35.540
He said, you know what?
他说，你知道吗？

1256
00:52:35.640 --> 00:52:37.400
Earlier today, the office needed Santa.
今天早些时候，办公室需要圣诞老人。

1257
00:52:37.640 --> 00:52:39.160
Then they needed another Santa.
然后他们需要另一个圣诞老人。

1258
00:52:39.300 --> 00:52:40.140
Then they needed Jesus.
然后他们需要耶稣。

1259
00:52:40.140 --> 00:52:41.660
And now they need Michael.
现在他们需要迈克尔。

1260
00:52:42.000 --> 00:52:44.360
And that's one suit Phyllis can't fit into.
而那是菲莉丝根本穿不下的衣服。

1261
00:52:45.560 --> 00:52:49.260
At 14 minutes, 38 seconds, I'd like to point out a snow alert.
在14分38秒时，我想指出一个大雪警报。

1262
00:52:49.680 --> 00:52:51.060
There is now...
现在有……

1263
00:52:51.060 --> 00:52:52.480
Do we have a snow alert?
我们有大雪警报吗？

1264
00:52:52.580 --> 00:52:53.440
We have a snow alert.
我们有大雪警报。

1265
00:52:54.520 --> 00:52:59.940
There is some snow falling gently behind Michael out his window.
迈克尔窗外正静静飘落着一些雪。

1266
00:53:00.380 --> 00:53:04.500
It's evening now, and it's begun snowing.
现在已经是傍晚了，开始下雪了。

1267
00:53:04.500 --> 00:53:06.540
This will be important later.
这在后面会很重要。

1268
00:53:07.360 --> 00:53:10.580
Well, the way you solve any crisis is you buy pizza.
嗯，解决任何危机的方法就是买披萨。

1269
00:53:11.060 --> 00:53:11.720
Lots of it.
买很多。

1270
00:53:12.180 --> 00:53:15.140
Michael's going to send Dwight with his password.
迈克尔打算派德怀特拿着他的密码去。

1271
00:53:15.460 --> 00:53:18.660
You know, you have fun at the...
你知道的，你们在……玩得开心

1272
00:53:20.560 --> 00:53:21.240
Yeah.
好嘞。

1273
00:53:21.380 --> 00:53:25.460
So his PIN is 9622.
所以他的密码是9622。

1274
00:53:26.040 --> 00:53:27.740
That is YMCA.
也就是YMCA。

1275
00:53:28.280 --> 00:53:34.300
The candy bag had some really fun alternates for what Michael's PIN number might be.
糖果袋里有一些关于迈克尔密码可能是什么的非常有趣的备选项。

1276
00:53:34.500 --> 00:53:34.820
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

1277
00:53:35.500 --> 00:53:36.580
Here's the first one.
这是第一个。

1278
00:53:37.200 --> 00:53:41.340
I don't want to say it, but it's the year everyone was scared by Y2K.
我不想说，但那是每个人都被千年虫吓坏的年份。

1279
00:53:44.740 --> 00:53:45.540
Here's another one.
这是另一个。

1280
00:53:46.100 --> 00:53:49.760
I don't want to say it, but it's the year we partied like it's 1999.
我不想说，但那是我们狂欢得像1999年一样的年份。

1281
00:53:51.640 --> 00:53:52.560
Here's another one.
这是另一个。

1282
00:53:53.580 --> 00:53:57.540
I don't want to say it, but it's the first line in a famous song about the alphabet.
我不想说，但这是一首关于字母表的著名歌曲的第一句。

1283
00:53:59.340 --> 00:54:00.760
And then this was my favorite.
然后这是我最喜欢的。

1284
00:54:01.540 --> 00:54:03.020
When Dwight says, what is your PIN?
当德怀特问，你的密码是什么？

1285
00:54:03.280 --> 00:54:04.380
Michael was going to say,
迈克尔原本要说，

1286
00:54:04.500 --> 00:54:11.880
938-562-08771-6689-473.
938-562-08771-6689-473。

1287
00:54:12.820 --> 00:54:16.180
I was just going to be like this ridiculously long number.
我本来打算说这样一个荒谬的长数字。

1288
00:54:16.420 --> 00:54:20.340
Those were all of our candy bag must shoot alternates for this.
这些都是我们为这个镜头准备的糖果袋必拍备选项。

1289
00:54:20.580 --> 00:54:25.920
And we stayed with the shooting draft scripted YMCA.
而我们最后保留了拍摄剧本里写好的YMCA。

1290
00:54:27.060 --> 00:54:31.380
Aaron's going to ask Andy, what was he thinking, giving her all of those gifts?
艾伦要问安迪，他送她那么多礼物到底是怎么想的？

1291
00:54:31.640 --> 00:54:32.320
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

1292
00:54:32.420 --> 00:54:33.340
Andy's not going to give up.
安迪是不会放弃的。

1293
00:54:33.440 --> 00:54:34.560
He's not going to throw in the towel.
他不会认输的。

1294
00:54:34.820 --> 00:54:35.500
Not going to happen.
绝不可能。

1295
00:54:35.500 --> 00:54:36.580
No, he's not.
不，他不会。

1296
00:54:37.260 --> 00:54:39.600
And later on, I'm glad he didn't.
而且后来，我很高兴他没有放弃。

1297
00:54:40.480 --> 00:54:42.080
Michael addresses the group.
迈克尔向大家发表讲话。

1298
00:54:42.340 --> 00:54:43.740
He's got the pizza.
他拿着披萨。

1299
00:54:44.220 --> 00:54:45.520
It's sitting there.
它就放在那里。

1300
00:54:45.520 --> 00:54:47.740
I think we'd all like to eat it.
我想我们大家都很想吃它。

1301
00:54:47.860 --> 00:54:50.360
But of course, Michael has to give a big speech firSt.
但当然，迈克尔首先得发表慷慨激昂的演讲。

1302
00:54:50.940 --> 00:54:58.360
And then he does what only Michael can do, which is he tells everybody the news that he
然后他做了只有迈克尔才做得出来的事，那就是把那个

1303
00:54:58.360 --> 00:55:02.520
was supposed to keep to himself, which is that we're going out of business.
本该保密的秘密告诉了所有人，也就是我们要倒闭了。

1304
00:55:02.520 --> 00:55:06.340
Well, everyone has a pretty strong reaction to this news.
好吧，大家对这个消息的反应都相当强烈。

1305
00:55:06.680 --> 00:55:09.160
Dwight goes out and kicks the Christmas tree down.
德怀特走出去把圣诞树给踢倒了。

1306
00:55:10.280 --> 00:55:15.260
Ellie and Mindy shared on the commentary that the day we shot this scene when Dwight's
艾莉和敏迪在评论音轨里分享说，拍这场德怀特

1307
00:55:15.260 --> 00:55:20.420
kicking the tree down, the episode Niagara was airing that evening.
踢倒圣诞树的戏那天，那一集《尼亚加拉》正好在当晚播出。

1308
00:55:20.700 --> 00:55:24.800
And everyone wanted to wrap so we could get to Greg's to watch Niagara.
大家都想早点收工，好去格雷格家看《尼亚加拉》。

1309
00:55:25.140 --> 00:55:29.840
I guess Greg had invited the whole cast over for a viewing party.
我猜格雷格邀请了全体演员去他家开观影派对。

1310
00:55:29.840 --> 00:55:34.060
So I dug in my digital clutter, and I found the email invite.
于是我在我的数字杂物堆里翻找，找到了那封邮件邀请函。

1311
00:55:34.360 --> 00:55:35.120
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

1312
00:55:35.120 --> 00:55:37.400
I totally remember this viewing party, by the way.
顺便说一句，我对这个观影派对印象太深了。

1313
00:55:37.500 --> 00:55:37.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1314
00:55:38.060 --> 00:55:44.260
He says, hey, guys, please come to my house for a viewing party for Niagara at 730, October
他说，嘿，伙计们，10月8日晚上7点半

1315
00:55:44.260 --> 00:55:44.840
8th.
，请来我家参加《尼亚加拉》观影派对。

1316
00:55:45.000 --> 00:55:48.000
Dinner, and we will watch Jim and Pam get married.
有晚餐，我们一起看吉姆和帕姆结婚。

1317
00:55:48.480 --> 00:55:49.220
Love, Greg.
爱你们的，格雷格。

1318
00:55:49.820 --> 00:55:55.740
Well, he and his wife, Suzanne, threw this party that was almost like a wedding reception.
嗯，他和妻子苏珊办的这场派对简直就像个婚宴。

1319
00:55:56.340 --> 00:56:00.480
They had little M&Ms printed with Jim and Pam.
他们准备了印有吉姆和帕姆头像的小M&M巧克力。

1320
00:56:00.700 --> 00:56:03.180
And little napkins like you would get at a wedding.
还有你在婚礼上能见到的那种小纸巾。

1321
00:56:03.520 --> 00:56:03.820
Yes.
对啊。

1322
00:56:03.940 --> 00:56:05.480
It was so sweet.
太贴心了。

1323
00:56:06.060 --> 00:56:07.920
They had amazing food.
他们准备了超棒的食物。

1324
00:56:07.920 --> 00:56:09.460
It was really fun.
真的很有趣。

1325
00:56:09.740 --> 00:56:13.280
The tables had, you know, the little confetti you can sprinkle that had the little wedding
桌子上摆着，你知道的，那种可以撒上去的带有

1326
00:56:13.280 --> 00:56:13.740
bells.
小婚礼钟图案的亮片碎屑。

1327
00:56:13.760 --> 00:56:15.020
It was so cute.
太可爱了。

1328
00:56:15.300 --> 00:56:17.120
I totally remember going to that.
我完全记得当时去了那儿。

1329
00:56:17.240 --> 00:56:17.860
I went with Lee.
我是和李一起去的。

1330
00:56:18.360 --> 00:56:23.260
So just know, while we were filming this conference room scene of Michael spilling the beans and
所以你们要知道，当我们正在拍会议室这场戏，也就是迈克尔说漏嘴、

1331
00:56:23.260 --> 00:56:27.020
Dwight kicking the tree, we were like, all right, let's get these lines so we can make
德怀特踢倒树的时候，我们心里都在想，行了，快把这些台词过了，好去

1332
00:56:27.020 --> 00:56:27.780
it to Greg's.
格雷格家。

1333
00:56:27.940 --> 00:56:29.980
Greg and Suzanne were always so generous.
格雷格和苏珊一直都那么大方慷慨。

1334
00:56:30.380 --> 00:56:35.480
They invited us into their home many, many times over these nine years of doing The Office.
在拍《办公室》的这九年里，他们多次邀请我们去他们家里做客。

1335
00:56:35.640 --> 00:56:40.240
It was a really warm and personal touch, and it bonded us from the beginning.
这是一种非常温馨而个人化的举动，从一开始就把我们紧紧联系在了一起。

1336
00:56:40.580 --> 00:56:41.420
It was really cool.
真的很酷。

1337
00:56:41.600 --> 00:56:42.560
And they still are.
而且他们现在依然如此。

1338
00:56:42.680 --> 00:56:45.580
Greg invited us all over for Sunday brunch, and we all went.
格雷格邀请我们大家去吃周日早午餐，我们都去了。

1339
00:56:45.740 --> 00:56:46.700
We did, just recently.
是的，就在最近。

1340
00:56:46.700 --> 00:56:47.380
Just recently.
就在最近。

1341
00:56:48.000 --> 00:56:52.920
Well, Michael tells everyone, listen, I'll get David on the phone so he can explain things.
好吧，迈克尔告诉大家，听着，我把大卫叫到电话上来，让他跟你们解释。

1342
00:56:53.200 --> 00:56:55.300
And Jim's like, I don't think so, Michael.
吉姆却说，我觉得不会吧，迈克尔。

1343
00:56:55.460 --> 00:56:58.160
I've been trying to reach him all day, and he's not taking my calls.
我一整天都在联系他，他根本不接我电话。

1344
00:56:58.780 --> 00:57:02.020
And Michael is like, I know how to get a hold of him.
而迈克尔则一副我知道怎么联系到他的样子。

1345
00:57:02.280 --> 00:57:02.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1346
00:57:02.700 --> 00:57:03.760
He's proud of this.
他为此感到挺自豪。

1347
00:57:03.880 --> 00:57:04.440
It's amazing.
这太绝了。

1348
00:57:04.880 --> 00:57:06.680
He knows where David's kids go to school.
他知道大卫的孩子在哪所学校上学。

1349
00:57:07.100 --> 00:57:10.620
So first he calls the school, pretends to be their pediatrician.
所以他先是打电话给学校，假装是孩子们的儿科医生。

1350
00:57:11.480 --> 00:57:17.240
Then he gets patched through to David's secretary, and then he talks in his little girl voice.
然后他被转接给了大卫的秘书，接着他用他的小女孩嗓音说话。

1351
00:57:17.240 --> 00:57:18.960
And pretends to be David's daughter.
并且假装是戴维的女儿。

1352
00:57:19.560 --> 00:57:23.980
So, of course, when David answers the phone, he's like, what's up, sweetie?
所以，当然，当戴维接电话时，他会说，怎么了，甜心？

1353
00:57:24.320 --> 00:57:24.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1354
00:57:24.920 --> 00:57:28.440
Because David thinks it's his daughter who's at the pediatrician's office.
因为戴维以为是他的女儿在儿科诊所。

1355
00:57:28.440 --> 00:57:30.200
Oh, my God, Michael.
哦，天哪，迈克尔。

1356
00:57:30.700 --> 00:57:32.120
I mean, it's kind of amazing.
我的意思是，这有点惊人。

1357
00:57:33.100 --> 00:57:39.040
In Michael's office, we have, for the first time, the whole entire Dunder Mifflin bullpen
在迈克尔的办公室里，我们第一次迎来了邓德米夫林的整个办公区

1358
00:57:39.040 --> 00:57:39.900
and warehouse.
和仓库。

1359
00:57:40.620 --> 00:57:40.900
Yes.
是的。

1360
00:57:41.380 --> 00:57:42.340
All of us.
我们所有人。

1361
00:57:42.760 --> 00:57:44.440
Hovering over the speakerphone.
都围在免提电话旁。

1362
00:57:44.960 --> 00:57:48.960
David reveals, Michael, first of all, you were never supposed to tell everybody.
戴维透露，迈克尔，首先，你本来就不应该把这件事告诉所有人。

1363
00:57:49.260 --> 00:57:51.700
But second of all, I wasn't talking about you.
但其次，我刚才不是在说你。

1364
00:57:52.420 --> 00:57:54.260
All of your jobs are safe.
你们所有人的工作都很安全。

1365
00:57:54.360 --> 00:57:56.180
It's just this upper management.
只是这群高层管理人员。

1366
00:57:56.600 --> 00:57:59.080
You would have thought the office won the Super Bowl.
你简直会以为办公室赢得超级碗了。

1367
00:57:59.240 --> 00:57:59.820
I know.
我知道。

1368
00:57:59.820 --> 00:58:02.200
So, everyone goes nuts.
所以，每个人都疯了。

1369
00:58:02.560 --> 00:58:06.420
Michael jumps off his desk and does this crowd surfing move.
迈克尔从他的办公桌上跳下来，做了个人群冲浪的动作。

1370
00:58:06.900 --> 00:58:11.600
Mindy shared on the commentary that that was Steve's idea, that he thought it would be
敏迪在解说中分享说那是史蒂夫的主意，他觉得

1371
00:58:11.600 --> 00:58:13.620
really fun if Michael dove into the crowd.
如果迈克尔跳进人群里会非常有趣。

1372
00:58:13.880 --> 00:58:15.840
We had a fan question from Kyle T.
我们收到了来自德克萨斯州休斯顿的凯尔·T.

1373
00:58:15.840 --> 00:58:20.220
in Houston, Texas, who said, did y'all have a safety meeting
的一个粉丝提问，他问，你们为迈克尔的人群跳水

1374
00:58:20.220 --> 00:58:21.840
for Michael's crowd dive?
开过安全会议吗？

1375
00:58:22.120 --> 00:58:25.060
By the way, I want you to know, Kyle wrote y'all.
顺便说一句，我想让你们知道，凯尔写信用了“y'all”（你们大家）。

1376
00:58:25.460 --> 00:58:26.280
Of course he did.
他当然会用了。

1377
00:58:26.360 --> 00:58:26.980
Kyle from Texas.
来自德克萨斯的凯尔。

1378
00:58:27.280 --> 00:58:27.600
That's right.
没错。

1379
00:58:27.720 --> 00:58:28.160
From Houston.
来自休斯顿。

1380
00:58:28.640 --> 00:58:29.340
H-Town.
H城。

1381
00:58:29.340 --> 00:58:31.980
Did y'all have a safety meeting for Michael's crowd dive?
你们为迈克尔的人群跳水开过安全会议吗？

1382
00:58:32.100 --> 00:58:33.660
I appreciated that detail, by the way.
顺便说一句，我很欣赏这个细节。

1383
00:58:34.060 --> 00:58:36.420
We did have a safety meeting.
我们确实开过安全会议。

1384
00:58:36.900 --> 00:58:43.820
Eric Sulke was our stunt coordinator, and Randy Cordray told us that he gave everyone direction
埃里克·苏尔克是我们的特技统筹，兰迪·科德雷告诉我们，他向每个人交代了

1385
00:58:43.820 --> 00:58:48.900
on how to catch Steve's dive and how to lower him down to the ground safely.
如何接住史蒂夫的跳水，以及如何安全地把他放低到地面上。

1386
00:58:49.280 --> 00:58:55.660
We also dressed two stunt players as warehouse workers and added them into the crowd.
我们还把两名特技演员打扮成仓库工人，把他们加到了人群中。

1387
00:58:55.660 --> 00:59:02.420
Randy said these burly stunt dudes were the main individuals involved in catching and protecting
兰迪说，这些身强力壮的特技猛男是负责接住和保护

1388
00:59:02.420 --> 00:59:05.180
Steve and keeping him from crashing to the floor.
史蒂夫并防止他摔到地板上的主力人员。

1389
00:59:05.360 --> 00:59:06.260
Yeah, it wasn't me.
是的，不是我。

1390
00:59:06.440 --> 00:59:09.900
It wasn't like me and Kate and you holding Steve up.
不是像我和凯特还有你把史蒂夫托起来那种。

1391
00:59:10.040 --> 00:59:10.400
Correct.
没错。

1392
00:59:10.400 --> 00:59:14.800
Now, folks, it's time for some karaoke.
现在，各位，是时候来点卡拉OK了。

1393
00:59:15.520 --> 00:59:15.840
Yeah.
耶。

1394
00:59:16.620 --> 00:59:22.220
This is where Dwight is singing Boulevard of Broken Dreams by Green Day.
这里是德怀特在唱绿日乐队的《Boulevard of Broken Dreams》（断梦大道）。

1395
00:59:22.540 --> 00:59:25.760
Andy joins in in some perfect harmony.
安迪加入进来，配合了完美的和声。

1396
00:59:26.360 --> 00:59:32.340
Boulevard of Broken Dreams is from Green Day's 2004 album American Idiot.
《Boulevard of Broken Dreams》出自绿日乐队2004年的专辑《American Idiot》（美国傻瓜）。

1397
00:59:32.340 --> 00:59:38.200
So, something that I know, because I'm friends with Billy Joe Armstrong, I cannot say it enough.
所以，我所知道的事实是，因为我和比利·乔·阿姆斯朋是朋友，我怎么说都不嫌多。

1398
00:59:38.240 --> 00:59:39.060
She's blushing again.
她又脸红了。

1399
00:59:39.060 --> 00:59:41.200
I'm just so tickled every time I can say that.
每次我能说出这句话，我都觉得高兴极了。

1400
00:59:41.200 --> 00:59:41.780
She's blushing again.
她又脸红了。

1401
00:59:41.780 --> 00:59:54.260
Is that Billy had seen The Office, but he recently, in 2019, did a big rewatch of the whole series.
比利以前看过《办公室》，不过他最近在2019年把整部剧重温了一遍。

1402
00:59:54.440 --> 00:59:55.120
Oh, nice.
哦，太棒了。

1403
00:59:55.500 --> 01:00:03.000
And I asked him, when you did your rewatch, did you remember that you had given us permission to use this song?
我问他，当你重温的时候，你还记得你曾经授权我们使用这首歌吗？

1404
01:00:03.800 --> 01:00:05.140
Here's what he had to say.
以下是他的回应。

1405
01:00:05.140 --> 01:00:21.920
I was binge watching The Office for the first time, and I was watching that episode, and then all of a sudden, the song came on, and I was completely taken by surprise.
我当时第一次狂刷《办公室》，正好看到了那一集，然后突然之间，这首歌就放出来了，我完全吓了一跳。

1406
01:00:23.140 --> 01:00:39.160
And, like, I think my face started to get red, and then Andy, he started singing harmonies, which was almost like the—because we do have a musical for American Idiot,
而且，我觉得我的脸开始变红，然后安迪，他开始唱起和声，这简直就像是——因为我们确实为《美国痴呆儿》做过一部音乐剧，

1407
01:00:39.240 --> 01:00:43.360
and he sang the same exact harmony that's in the musical.
他唱的和音乐剧里的和声一模一样。

1408
01:00:43.620 --> 01:00:46.220
So, it was good.
所以，这很不错。

1409
01:00:46.620 --> 01:00:51.180
Well, I just love it that he was surprised by his own song during that rewatch.
嗯，我特别喜欢他在重温时被自己的歌吓到这一点。

1410
01:00:51.180 --> 01:00:51.580
I know.
我知道。

1411
01:00:51.700 --> 01:00:52.440
That's so sweet.
太可爱了。

1412
01:00:52.720 --> 01:00:55.000
Listen, I think we need to hear this.
听着，我觉得我们得听听这个。

1413
01:00:55.180 --> 01:00:58.600
I think we need to hear Dwight and Andy singing Boulevard of Broken DreaMs.
我觉得我们需要听听德怀特和安迪唱《断梦大道》。

1414
01:00:58.760 --> 01:00:59.420
Oh, for sure.
哦，那当然。

1415
01:01:00.720 --> 01:01:05.820
Walk a lonely road, only one that I have ever known.
走一条孤独的路，我所知道的唯一一条。

1416
01:01:06.380 --> 01:01:11.640
Don't know where it goes, but it's all to me, and I walk alone.
不知道它通往何方，但它对我而言就是全部，我独自前行。

1417
01:01:12.660 --> 01:01:13.300
It's true.
确实如此。

1418
01:01:13.480 --> 01:01:13.760
Yes.
是的。

1419
01:01:14.380 --> 01:01:15.540
We all walk alone.
我们都在独自前行。

1420
01:01:28.010 --> 01:01:28.710
Beside me.
就在我身边。

1421
01:01:31.310 --> 01:01:32.130
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1422
01:01:32.230 --> 01:01:33.090
I love hearing them.
我爱听他们唱。

1423
01:01:33.210 --> 01:01:34.810
I could hear them do it, like, every day.
我每天都想听他们唱。

1424
01:01:34.810 --> 01:01:36.930
It would make me happy singing that song.
唱这首歌会让我感到快乐。

1425
01:01:37.610 --> 01:01:46.970
Mindy shared in the commentary that she absolutely loved this montage of Christmas kind of all coming together, set to the backdrop of a non-Christmas song.
敏迪在解说中分享说，她非常喜欢这个圣诞节各种事物融合在一起的蒙太奇，背景音乐是一首非圣诞歌曲。

1426
01:01:47.110 --> 01:01:47.350
Yes.
没错。

1427
01:01:47.350 --> 01:01:55.770
And Jenna, I guess there was a musical interlude to the karaoke, and Ed and Rain had to vamp during it.
珍娜，我猜卡拉OK中间有一段音乐插曲，埃德和雷恩在期间不得不即兴发挥。

1428
01:01:55.810 --> 01:01:56.910
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

1429
01:01:57.130 --> 01:01:59.170
It's in the extended producer's cut.
这在制片人加长版里有。

1430
01:01:59.350 --> 01:02:00.930
We have to hear their vamp.
我们必须听听他们的即兴表演。

1431
01:02:24.120 --> 01:02:29.020
I mean, I know they already produced the musical version of American Idiot.
我的意思是，我知道他们已经制作了音乐剧版的《美国痴呆儿》。

1432
01:02:29.020 --> 01:02:34.000
But I'm saying, if you bring it back to the stage, you might want to add this.
但我的意思是，如果你把它搬回舞台，你可能想加上这个。

1433
01:02:34.400 --> 01:02:35.140
Ed and Rain.
埃德和雷恩。

1434
01:02:35.680 --> 01:02:37.680
You might want to, because it's pretty great.
你可能真得加上，因为这太棒了。

1435
01:02:37.920 --> 01:02:39.000
We've all been there.
我们都经历过。

1436
01:02:39.080 --> 01:02:40.680
We've all picked a song for karaoke.
我们都为卡拉OK选过歌。

1437
01:02:40.680 --> 01:02:42.700
And then there's a big musical interlude.
然后中间会有一段很大的音乐插曲。

1438
01:02:42.740 --> 01:02:43.860
And you're like, what do I do?
你会想，我该怎么办？

1439
01:02:44.160 --> 01:02:44.480
Yes.
对啊。

1440
01:02:44.660 --> 01:02:45.780
I'm just kind of bobbing my head.
我就只能在那儿晃晃脑袋。

1441
01:02:45.780 --> 01:02:48.300
Ed, I mean, Ed crushed it.
埃德，我是说，埃德太拿捏了。

1442
01:02:48.720 --> 01:02:54.940
Well, there are just a bunch of scenes now of people enjoying Christmas.
好吧，现在有一堆大家享受圣诞节的场景。

1443
01:02:55.480 --> 01:02:58.800
Everyone's getting gifts that are really meaningful to them.
每个人都得到了对他们来说意义重大的礼物。

1444
01:02:59.240 --> 01:03:07.860
And finally, Dwight is going to get the last piece of his gift and realizes this whole time he's been making a nutcracker.
最后，德怀特终于得到了他礼物的最后一部分，并意识到他这一整天都在做一个胡桃夹子。

1445
01:03:08.360 --> 01:03:09.660
Yes, of course.
对，当然。

1446
01:03:09.660 --> 01:03:12.360
It's like a really cool nutcracker.
这就像一个超级酷的胡桃夹子。

1447
01:03:12.360 --> 01:03:15.760
We had a fan question from Lacey L.
我们收到了来自德克萨斯州大草原城的莱西·L的粉丝提问。

1448
01:03:15.940 --> 01:03:17.780
in Grand Prairie, Texas.
求求你，快跟我讲讲德怀特的胡桃夹子。

1449
01:03:18.300 --> 01:03:21.140
Please, please tell me about Dwight's nutcracker.
这是谁想出来的点子？

1450
01:03:21.380 --> 01:03:22.360
Who came up with it?
这是谁想出来的？

1451
01:03:22.480 --> 01:03:23.680
Where did they find it?
他们是在哪里找到它的？

1452
01:03:23.780 --> 01:03:25.180
Or did they have to create it?
还是说他们必须凭空创造？

1453
01:03:25.320 --> 01:03:27.600
I have been looking for it for years.
我已经找了好多年了。

1454
01:03:27.920 --> 01:03:29.360
Lacey, I thought the same thing.
莱西，我也是这么想的。

1455
01:03:29.580 --> 01:03:31.060
I thought, can I get one of these?
我想，我也能弄到一个吗？

1456
01:03:31.680 --> 01:03:36.080
Well, Randy told me that this was not in the first shooting draft of the script.
嗯，兰迪告诉我，这并不在剧本的第一版拍摄初稿里。

1457
01:03:36.080 --> 01:03:44.380
This whole runner was added later, and he believes that it was the master of the cold opens, Aaron Schur, who wrote this story arc.
这个贯穿整集的桥段是后来加的，他相信是冷场开场之王亚伦·舒尔写了这条故事线。

1458
01:03:44.520 --> 01:03:49.620
Because Aaron became the point person that they went to to discuss the creation of this prop.
因为亚伦成了他们讨论这个道具制作时去找的核心人物。

1459
01:03:50.100 --> 01:03:57.460
Randy said when he and Phil first read this story arc, they assumed that this contraption was something the writers had seen on the internet somewhere.
兰迪说，当他和菲尔第一次读到这个故事线时，他们以为这个玩意儿是编剧们在网上的某个地方看到的。

1460
01:03:57.800 --> 01:03:59.980
And they wanted to know where do they buy it.
他们想知道在哪里能买到。

1461
01:04:00.500 --> 01:04:03.040
It turns out, Ange, it did not exist anywhere.
结果证明，安琪，这东西根本不存在。

1462
01:04:03.520 --> 01:04:04.600
They made it up?
他们是凭空捏造的？

1463
01:04:04.600 --> 01:04:06.640
Yeah, they made it up.
对，他们是凭空捏造的。

1464
01:04:06.780 --> 01:04:12.060
I even went to the rewrite of the script, and there is no scripted description of this machine.
我甚至去查了剧本的改写版，上面对这台机器没有任何剧本描述。

1465
01:04:12.880 --> 01:04:26.120
So Phil needed to conceptualize, design, and build a working nutcracker prop that looked like it could have been a gun, and he had less than a week to do it.
所以菲尔需要构思、设计并制造一个能工作的胡桃夹子道具，它看起来还得像一把枪，而他只有不到一周的时间来完成。

1466
01:04:26.320 --> 01:04:27.020
Phil Shay.
菲尔·谢伊。

1467
01:04:27.540 --> 01:04:30.280
This is why he was always running, folks.
这就是为什么他总是那么匆忙，各位。

1468
01:04:30.460 --> 01:04:30.820
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1469
01:04:30.820 --> 01:04:36.120
Phil went to his go-to props manufacturing house, the hand prop room.
菲尔去了他最常去的道具制造厂——手工道具室。

1470
01:04:36.460 --> 01:04:44.140
The team at that facility, Randy said, was understandably freaked out at the very short time span that they had to create this prop.
兰迪说，那里的团队对于他们只有这么短的时间来制作这个道具，感到恐慌也是情理之中。

1471
01:04:44.560 --> 01:04:49.220
They told Phil to tell Randy to open up the company checkbook.
他们让菲尔转告兰迪打开公司的支票簿。

1472
01:04:49.480 --> 01:04:54.800
They were going to have to put a full team of engineers and builders basically around the clock to get this done in time.
他们不得不安排一整支由工程师和制造人员组成的队伍连轴转，以便按时完成这件作品。

1473
01:04:54.800 --> 01:04:58.160
Randy said to their credit, they did a masterful job.
兰迪说，值得称赞的是，他们完成得非常出色。

1474
01:04:58.340 --> 01:05:01.820
All in, this prop cost about $19,000.
总计下来，这个道具花费大约一万九千美元。

1475
01:05:02.980 --> 01:05:05.100
Also, it was a one-off.
而且，这是独一无二的孤品。

1476
01:05:05.700 --> 01:05:13.300
He said, to the best of his knowledge, the NBC Universal marketing people never made replicas of this for online sales.
他说，据他所知，NBC环球的营销人员从未制作过这东西的复制品用于网上销售。

1477
01:05:13.540 --> 01:05:14.580
They should have.
他们本该做的。

1478
01:05:14.900 --> 01:05:15.900
They still can.
他们现在还可以做。

1479
01:05:15.980 --> 01:05:17.160
I'm just saying.
我只是随便说说。

1480
01:05:17.160 --> 01:05:19.800
This would be a hot item at the holidays.
这在节假日会是个大热销的商品。

1481
01:05:20.000 --> 01:05:20.220
Yeah.
对啊。

1482
01:05:20.440 --> 01:05:22.280
Do you know how many people would buy this?
你知道会有多少人买这个吗？

1483
01:05:22.400 --> 01:05:22.960
I would.
我会买。

1484
01:05:22.960 --> 01:05:23.920
I would, too.
我也会买。

1485
01:05:24.560 --> 01:05:26.140
But do I have to put it together?
但我还得自己把它组装起来吗？

1486
01:05:26.720 --> 01:05:27.380
Oh, no.
哦，不。

1487
01:05:27.440 --> 01:05:27.880
Oh, no.
哦，不。

1488
01:05:28.080 --> 01:05:28.920
What if you do?
如果非要你组装呢？

1489
01:05:28.940 --> 01:05:30.160
That would be the ultimate.
那可真是绝了。

1490
01:05:30.500 --> 01:05:30.940
I know.
我知道。

1491
01:05:31.240 --> 01:05:36.460
You know, this story reminds me of something that I had a makeup artist tell me once.
你知道，这个故事让我想起了一位化妆师曾经对我说过的话。

1492
01:05:37.040 --> 01:05:40.260
She said, there is a saying in this business.
她说，这个行业里有一句俗语。

1493
01:05:41.140 --> 01:05:44.060
It's called fast, cheap, or good.
叫做快、便宜或好。

1494
01:05:44.500 --> 01:05:47.140
And you can only have two of the three things.
你只能三者取其二。

1495
01:05:47.640 --> 01:05:50.820
It can be fast and cheap, but it's not going to look good.
它可以又快又便宜，但看起来不会好。

1496
01:05:51.300 --> 01:05:54.120
It can be cheap and good, but it's not going to be faSt.
它可以便宜又好，但它不会快。

1497
01:05:54.700 --> 01:05:58.880
If you want it to be both fast and good, it's not going to be cheap.
如果你想让它既快又好，那它就不会便宜。

1498
01:05:59.620 --> 01:06:01.260
That was the case with our Nutcracker.
我们的胡桃夹子就是这种情况。

1499
01:06:01.860 --> 01:06:02.780
Fast and good.
又快又好。

1500
01:06:03.140 --> 01:06:04.000
It was not cheap.
它可不便宜。

1501
01:06:04.020 --> 01:06:04.900
Not going to be cheap.
这可不便宜。

1502
01:06:05.060 --> 01:06:05.240
Nope.
没错。

1503
01:06:05.240 --> 01:06:10.940
Well, Jenna Mindy also spoke about this scene on the commentary, and she said it was a last-minute
詹娜·明迪也在评论音轨中谈到了这个场景，她说这是最后关头

1504
01:06:10.940 --> 01:06:13.340
rewrite, that it was not in her original draft.
重写出来的，她最初的初稿里并没有。

1505
01:06:13.560 --> 01:06:16.720
She said it was written by Aaron Schur and Charlie Grandy.
她说这是由亚伦·舒尔和查理·格兰迪写的。

1506
01:06:17.200 --> 01:06:23.040
And Mindy said Phil Shea went above and beyond, especially because it was a last-minute prop
明迪还说菲尔·希亚付出了超常的努力，特别是因为这是一个临时决定的道具

1507
01:06:23.040 --> 01:06:23.340
gag.
恶作剧。

1508
01:06:23.700 --> 01:06:28.580
She also commented that it was a note from Greg to add a Dwight Michael storyline to this
她还提到，格雷格提出意见，要在这一集中加入一条德怀特和迈克尔的故事线，

1509
01:06:28.580 --> 01:06:31.700
episode, and it pays off so nicely at the end.
最后的效果非常棒。

1510
01:06:31.700 --> 01:06:33.920
And it's a moment of redemption for Michael.
这也是迈克尔完成自我救赎的时刻。

1511
01:06:34.600 --> 01:06:35.000
Yes.
是的。

1512
01:06:35.440 --> 01:06:35.920
Yeah.
对。

1513
01:06:36.040 --> 01:06:37.900
He knows Dwight so well.
他太了解德怀特了。

1514
01:06:38.260 --> 01:06:38.720
Yeah.
对。

1515
01:06:38.960 --> 01:06:39.660
It's a good note.
这是个好主意。

1516
01:06:39.940 --> 01:06:40.380
Yeah.
是的。

1517
01:06:41.180 --> 01:06:43.200
Well, the party is wrapping up.
好了，派对要结束了。

1518
01:06:43.320 --> 01:06:44.760
Everyone is leaving for the night.
大家都准备回家了。

1519
01:06:44.960 --> 01:06:47.180
They're walking out into the parking lot.
他们正走向停车场。

1520
01:06:47.320 --> 01:06:48.040
There's snow.
下雪了。

1521
01:06:48.040 --> 01:06:50.360
It feels so Christmassy and festive.
感觉充满了圣诞气氛和节日氛围。

1522
01:06:51.220 --> 01:06:52.060
That's right.
没错。

1523
01:06:52.300 --> 01:06:56.280
You know, as you're walking out, Angela, I don't know if you noticed this, but we got
安吉拉，当你们走出去的时候，我不知道你有没有注意到，我们收到了

1524
01:06:56.280 --> 01:06:59.620
a fan question from Kelsey D in Orlando, Florida.
来自佛罗里达州奥兰多的凯尔西·D的粉丝提问。

1525
01:06:59.620 --> 01:07:06.060
I noticed when everyone is leaving the office, Angela slips, and Daryl is there to help her.
我注意到大家离开办公室时，安吉拉滑倒了，达里尔在那里扶了她一把。

1526
01:07:06.480 --> 01:07:09.420
Did Angela actually slip, or was that planned?
安吉拉是真的滑倒了，还是设计好的？

1527
01:07:09.480 --> 01:07:11.020
Because I love that moment.
因为我很喜欢那个时刻。

1528
01:07:11.200 --> 01:07:13.860
It's so cute and sweet between Angela and Daryl.
安吉拉和达里尔之间太可爱、太温馨了。

1529
01:07:14.580 --> 01:07:14.900
Okay.
好的。

1530
01:07:15.320 --> 01:07:20.340
Kelsey, I did actually trip, and I grabbed Craig's arm.
凯尔西，我其实是真的绊了一下，然后抓住了克雷格的手臂。

1531
01:07:20.460 --> 01:07:23.980
So that quick moment you're seeing, that's us.
所以你看到的那个短暂瞬间，其实是我们真实的反应。

1532
01:07:24.220 --> 01:07:24.680
Aw.
噢。

1533
01:07:24.680 --> 01:07:31.000
We're not in character, and I think Rain must have seen it and improvised the line as Dwight,
我们当时没在演角色，我想雷恩一定看到了，于是即兴说了一句德怀特的台词：小心，外面很滑，因为剧本里根本没有这句台词。

1534
01:07:31.240 --> 01:07:36.080
watch out, it's slippery out here, because that line is not in the shooting draft.
我滑倒和绊倒当然也不在拍摄剧本里。

1535
01:07:36.320 --> 01:07:39.520
Me slipping and tripping is obviously not in the shooting draft.
所以，是的，那纯粹是我和克雷格，谢天谢地他在那儿，因为我当时好像扭到脚踝了什么的。

1536
01:07:39.820 --> 01:07:45.600
So, yes, that's just me and Craig, and thank goodness he was there, because I guess I turned
好吧，突然之间，我们听到了一些声音。

1537
01:07:45.600 --> 01:07:46.700
my ankle or something.
是鼓手。

1538
01:07:46.700 --> 01:07:49.240
Well, all of a sudden, we hear something.
是敲击大鼓的十二名鼓手！

1539
01:07:49.660 --> 01:07:51.060
It's drummers.
这是安迪送给艾伦的最后一份圣诞礼物。

1540
01:07:51.620 --> 01:07:54.460
It's 12 drummers drumming!
安迪在打镲。

1541
01:07:54.840 --> 01:07:58.120
This is Aaron's final Christmas present from Andy.
他开始跳起舞来。

1542
01:07:58.420 --> 01:08:00.320
Andy is on the cymbals.
太有节日气氛了。

1543
01:08:00.640 --> 01:08:02.220
He starts dancing.
我们收到了来自亚利桑那州凤凰城的瑞秋·I的粉丝反馈，她说，

1544
01:08:02.220 --> 01:08:03.880
It's so festive.
仪仗队里只有11个人。

1545
01:08:04.620 --> 01:08:09.160
We had a fan catch from Rachel I in Phoenix, Arizona, who said,
安迪原本是第12个人吗？

1546
01:08:09.160 --> 01:08:12.080
There are only 11 people in the drumline.
是的，瑞秋。

1547
01:08:12.340 --> 01:08:14.920
Was Andy meant to be the 12th person?
他就是这个打击乐仪仗队里的第12名乐手。

1548
01:08:15.500 --> 01:08:16.760
Yes, Rachel.
我们还收到了玛丽亚·S的提问。

1549
01:08:16.760 --> 01:08:21.300
He was the 12th percussionist in this drumline.
我们要回答玛丽亚的问题。

1550
01:08:21.760 --> 01:08:24.220
We also got a question from Maria S.
玛丽亚·S问：

1551
01:08:24.380 --> 01:08:26.420
in Austin, Texas, who asked,
来自得克萨斯州奥斯汀的她问道，

1552
01:08:26.540 --> 01:08:31.020
What was the process for choosing this group that played the 12 drummers drumming?
